<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Smart Board Update Helper
  File name: updater-settings.xml

  Fill in the school and classroom prefix, then give this file to the installer
  with the helper app. The app reads it and fills in the school.
  The installer only types the classroom number.

  How to use it
  1. Keep this file named updater-settings.xml. Do not rename it.
  2. Type the school name between the school tags.
  3. Type the classroom prefix between the classroom-prefix tags.
     The prefix is added in front of the number they type.
     Example: prefix "Room " and they type 102, the helper submits "Room 102".
     Leave a space at the end when the prefix is a word, such as "Room " or "Class ".
  4. Copy the file onto the phone or SMART board before opening the helper.
     Put it in the Download folder, or on the main storage of the phone.
     A USB stick also works if the stick is plugged in and the file is in the root or in Download.
  5. Open Smart Board Update Helper.
     The school name is filled in and cannot be changed on that device.
  6. They tap Submit. The office still has to approve that room before any update can install.
     This file does not unlock a board.

  What to edit
  - school: the school name shown on the helper and sent for approval.
  - classroom-prefix: the text placed in front of the classroom number.
-->
<updater-settings>
  <school></school>
  <classroom-prefix></classroom-prefix>
</updater-settings>
